    "updated_at": "2026-10-07T16:45:01Z",
    "body": "For anyone wondering: using coding assistants, AI tools, or test automation as part of your own real development work is completely fine — that's just normal tooling.\n\nWhat's rejected is automated *claiming/submission* behavior — bots auto-posting `/claim`, `/opire try`, or similar bounty-bot commands, and PRs that were never actually built or tested against the real bug (placeholder comments, no evidence of a real boot, wrong repo/file entirely).\n\nThe bar is simple regardless of what tools you used to get there: a real root cause, a real fix, verified by an actual boot reaching a visible working desktop, with a screenshot or equivalent proof. However you arrive at that is your business.",
